///1VFILER
VFILER Version 1.2 - CP/M-86 File Manipulation Program
  Original ZCPR2 version by Rich Conn
  CP/M-86 translation by H. M. Van Tassell
  Optimized for IBM-compatibles by Kirk Lawrence

This patched version uses a VT100/ANSI terminal (80 columns,
24 rows). IBM keypad reprogramming is disabled.
Arrow keys accept ESC [ A/B/C/D and ESC O A/B/C/D.
PgUp uses ESC [ 5 ~; PgDn uses ESC [ 6 ~ (without spaces).
Q quits immediately. ESC quits after an inter-byte polling wait.
The wait duration depends on the CPU or emulator speed.
Control-key alternatives: ^K up, ^J down, ^L right, ^H left,
^W previous page, ^Z next page.

Select a topic for the available commands.

///2MOVEMENT
Use the ARROW keys (up, down, left, right) to move the
on-screen pointer (-->).

  Left arrow  - File Left
  Right arrow - File Right
  Up arrow    - File Up
  Down arrow  - File Down
  G           - Go To a File
  PGDN        - Screen Forward
  PGUP        - Screen Backward

Use PGUP and PGDN to move the screen up or down a page.

///2TAGGING
  T - Tag File
  U - Untag File
  W - Mass Tag/Untag

///2FILES
  C - Copy File
  D - Delete File
  F - File Size
  M - Mass Copy
  R - Rename File
  Y - Mass Delete

///2PRINTVIEW
  P - Print
  V - View

///2MISC
  O        - shOw System Files
  E        - Enter Command
  L        - Login DIR
  N        - reNew Screen
  S        - Status of Disk
  ESC or Q - Quit VFILER
  ENTER    - Execute a CMD file

